WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.284 --> 00:00:03.794
Getting an AI agent to work with
your company's data can be tricky.

2
00:00:04.418 --> 00:00:06.398
Your data lives in OneLake.

3
00:00:06.368 --> 00:00:10.168
Connecting your agent to it,
in a way your IT team can approve,

4
00:00:10.138 --> 00:00:10.958
is the hard part.

5
00:00:11.537 --> 00:00:13.502
Krusgraph is the bridge.

6
00:00:13.472 --> 00:00:15.732
Sign in with Microsoft Entra.

7
00:00:15.702 --> 00:00:17.232
Krusgraph reads your tables

8
00:00:17.202 --> 00:00:19.492
with your permissions and
maps how they connect.

9
00:00:20.073 --> 00:00:21.883
Then it checks that map against your data.

10
00:00:22.539 --> 00:00:25.109
From one checked plan,
you get what you need:

11
00:00:25.079 --> 00:00:30.329
a report, a semantic model, an API,
and an ontology your agents can use.

12
00:00:30.961 --> 00:00:32.780
Everything is read-only by default,

13
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.890
and you see a dry run
before anything is created.

14
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.800
Your agent. Your data. Connected.

15
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.520
Krusgraph, for Microsoft Fabric.
